    "q-75663": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75663",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, and ${I}_{4}$ is the $4\\times 4$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A$\n\nII. $(CA)B=C(AB)$\n\nIII. $BC=CB$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{4}={I}_{4}A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is asociative, so $(CA)B=C(AB)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $BC\\ne CB$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I  and II are true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75663-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "html": "I and II only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75663-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II only",
              "html": "II only"
            },
            {
